          "content": "104"
        },
        {
          "type": "header",
          "bbox": [
            0.186,
            0.071,
            0.494,
            0.089
          ],
          "content": "Ganita Manjari | Grade 9 | Part II"
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph_title",
          "bbox": [
            0.136,
            0.114,
            0.399,
            0.137
          ],
          "level": 2,
          "content": "Think and Reflect"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.132,
            0.154,
            0.854,
            0.213
          ],
          "content": "The cost of one paratha and 2 bowls of dahi is ₹90. Also, the cost of 2 parathas and 7 bowls of dahi is ₹260. Can you figure out the cost of one paratha and one bowl of dahi and explain your reasoning?"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.116,
            0.238,
            0.883,
            0.317
          ],
          "content": "Do you remember Rakesh’s puzzle from Grade 7 ? “I have thought of two numbers”, he said. “Their sum is 25 and their difference is 11”. We solved the problem by making a table and listing possible combinations. We can also solve this using a pair of linear equations."
        },
        {
          "type": "table",
          "bbox": [
            0.183,
            0.322,
            0.816,
            0.469
          ],
          "content": "| First Number | Second Number | Sum | Difference |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| 10 | 15 | 25 | -5 |\n| 20 | 5 | 25 | 15 |\n| 18 | 7 | 25 | 11 |",
          "captions": [],
          "footnotes": [],
          "image_source": "images/page_19_table_5.jpg"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.152,
            0.485,
            0.732,
            0.507
          ],
          "content": "If the two numbers are x and y, we get the equations"
        },
        {
          "type": "equation",
          "bbox": [
            0.367,
            0.512,
            0.628,
            0.533
          ],
          "content": "x + y = 25   and   x - y = 11.",
          "image_source": "images/page_19_equation_7.jpg"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.116,
            0.538,
            0.882,
            0.615
          ],
          "content": "Such problems lead to a **pair of linear equations in two variables**. A solution to such a pair of equations is an ordered pair (a, b) that satisfies both equations. How do we find a solution? We shall soon see."
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.116,
            0.615,
            0.882,
            0.674
          ],
          "content": "Consider another situation. A science exhibition charges an entry fee that is different for adults and children. Here are the amount paid by two different groups."
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.152,
            0.677,
            0.71,
            0.698
          ],
          "content": "**Group A:** 2 adult tickets and 3 child tickets for ₹600"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.153,
            0.702,
            0.709,
            0.723
          ],
          "content": "**Group B:** 3 adult tickets and 2 child tickets for ₹700"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.153,
            0.727,
            0.727,
            0.748
          ],
          "content": "How much do individual adult and child tickets cost?"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.153,
            0.752,
            0.851,
            0.773
          ],
          "content": "If the cost of one adult ticket is ₹x and one child ticket is ₹y, then:"
        },
        {
          "type": "equation",
          "bbox": [
            0.351,
            0.779,
            0.646,
            0.799
          ],
          "content": "2x+3y=600,3x+2y=700.",
          "image_source": "images/page_19_equation_14.jpg"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.152,
            0.805,
            0.828,
            0.825
          ],
          "content": "This gives us another pair of linear equations in two variables."
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.117,
            0.825,
            0.88,
            0.865
          ],
          "content": "A solution to these equations will give us the answer that we seek. Can you see why?"
        }
      ]
    }
  ],
